Honour whisper_context_params.use_coreml (see whisper.h.patch) when loading the
Core ML encoder, and fix a %ld/size_t format mismatch that warns on Apple targets.

Hexagon (ggml-hexagon) support, needed until the equivalent lands upstream:
- weight_buft_supported: only the CPU buffer type is accepted unconditionally.
  GPU-class devices (Hexagon reports itself as GPU) are probed with
  supports_op, so ops the backend cannot run on quantized/repacked weights
  (GET_ROWS on token_embd, unsupported MUL_MAT types) fall back to the CPU
  buffer instead of asserting at graph time.
- Mark model buffers as GGML_BACKEND_BUFFER_USAGE_WEIGHTS right after
  allocation so backends that repack weights on set_tensor (Hexagon) see the
  usage flag while the tensors are being uploaded.
- Write the KV caches with ggml_set_rows instead of ggml_cpy when flash
  attention is on (encoder kv_pad, cross-attention kv_cross, decoder kv_self).
  The cpy form reshapes and converts f32 -> f16 in one op, which Hexagon's CPY
  kernel does not support; set_rows is what llama.cpp uses for the same job.
  The row indices are graph inputs filled after ggml_backend_sched_alloc_graph.
- whisper_log_callback_default keeps dropping GGML_LOG_LEVEL_DEBUG unless
  WHISPER_LOG_DEBUG is set (GGML_HEXAGON_PROFILE=1 logs at that level).
- Model / VAD loaders: fail the load when a weight buffer cannot be allocated
  (Hexagon's fastrpc_mmap can fail, e.g. when the DSP cannot map more memory).
  Upstream skips the NULL buffer and later aborts in
  ggml_backend_buffer_is_host while reading the weights. llama.cpp's loader
  also treats this as a load error. The failure path now uses whisper_free so
  buffers allocated before the failing one (e.g. the CPU half of a q8_0 model)
  are released instead of leaked.
- whisper_state::batch is value-initialized. whisper_init_state calls
  whisper_free_state when a backend, KV cache or compute buffer cannot be
  allocated, which runs before whisper_batch_init and used to free the
  uninitialized batch pointers (scudo abort on Android).
